      "statement": "AA Intelligence Index v4.3.2 live board 2026-10-07 (cost per index task in parentheses): Opus 5.5 max 57.62 ($5.98), Sonnet 5.5 max 56.00 ($7.67), Opus 5.5 xhigh 55.99 ($3.46), Opus 5.5 high 53.58 ($1.82), Astra max 52.67 ($3.26), Sonnet 5.5 xhigh 51.90 ($2.75), GPT-6.1 Sol max 51.83 ($0.72), Sol xhigh 51.04 ($0.39), Sol high 50.24 ($0.32), Sol medium 47.78 ($0.21), Sonnet 5.5 high 46.75 ($1.12), Opus 5.5 medium 51.24 ($1.34). Comparison with the 55 stored same-model, same-effort AA v4.3.2 rows (2026-09-22..29): 50 agree to the stored precision; the 5 that differ are GPT-6 Luna (max 37.26 -> 38.12, medium 29.46 -> 29.93, low 20.92 -> 21.53) and Sonnet 5.5 medium (40.74 on 2026-09-29 -> 40.84), i.e. AA appears to have re-scored Luna and Sonnet 5.5 slightly; every shift is below one index point.",
      "implication": "On AA, GPT-6.1 Sol high (50.24, $0.32) is 1.0 index point below Opus 5.5 medium (51.24, $1.34) at about a quarter of the cost per task; Sol max (51.83, $0.72) is 1.75 below Opus 5.5 high (53.58, $1.82) at about 40% of the cost.",
